  "description": "HALHIO crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C78 H120 Co8 Gd4 N8 O38 4+,4(Cl1 O4 1-),2(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co4 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Co5 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co6 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co7 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co8 (Co) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 24 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.115-3.973 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 83.01-114.08°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Gd4Co8(OH)8(hmp)8(O2CEt)8(MeOH)6](ClO4)4. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
